WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.967
A working calculator cover. The app stays behind its access gate.

2
00:00:04.967 --> 00:00:09.433
Choose what a shake opens: tile puzzle, calculator, weather or grocery list.

3
00:00:09.433 --> 00:00:17.400
An emulated shake switches the app to its weather cover. Weather readings are sample data.

4
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:24.400
Set a local master password for protected sections. The password stays masked.

5
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:30.833
Choose which sections require the master password: Q-Note, Q-Pass and Q-Chat.

6
00:00:30.833 --> 00:00:37.300
Q-Note shows a locked screen. Unlock it to load the private notes and previews.

7
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:47.300
Type a draft with Quantum Keyboard. Its tools stay in the keyboard toolbar. Demo contact offline; message not sent.

8
00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:51.600
Separate fields for the primary PIN, duress wipe and decoy vault. Configuration only; no duress action triggered.

9
00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:57.567
Review what Factory Wipe removes and its limits. The confirmation remains unchecked; no wipe is executed.
